\subsection{Displacement, attitude and sensor-bias reconstruction}
Figures~\ref{fig:csm-validation-kinematics}--\ref{fig:csm-validation-bias}
use the medium JONSWAP record, $H_s=1.5$~m, and wave/IMU/initialization
seeds 11/101/1009. The position, velocity, acceleration and attitude examples
show the final 60~s. Bias and adaptation plots retain the complete 1200~s
to expose convergence and the startup holds. The plotting harness uses a
vertical-up convention; the method equations use NED. The released records
have constant yaw, and the harness expresses the plotted reference in its
magnetic heading gauge. The yaw panel therefore tests magnetic alignment
and drift on that heading, not arbitrary vessel-turn performance.
