\subsection{Rendering and reproducibility}
All metrics and seed resampling precede plot decimation. Drawing traces
retain ordered coordinate extrema and endpoints using
\path{plots/vector_export.py}; they are capped at 2000 points per stored
trace. The same project exporter shares the point budget among overlaid
curves at SVG and PGF export. No score, spectrum, covariance statistic or
bootstrap sample is computed from those drawing traces. The compact traces
and full-rate per-run scores are committed; the original long replay CSVs
are regenerated when needed.
The run matrix, source and binary hashes, dataset checksums, fixed seed
triplets and scoring intervals are recorded in
\path{reports/results/carma_shared_modes_validation/protocol.json}.
